# LeakSanitizer suppressions for rhi_triangle_smoke in sanitizer builds (HELIOS_SANITIZE; wired in
# CMakeLists.txt). Every entry matches an allocation made inside an external library, below SDL's own
# initialisation; none can match Helios code (every reported stack is main -> run -> SDL_Init -> ...).
# Diagnosed with SDL 3.4.16, Mesa 25.2.8 (lavapipe), LLVM 20.1.2 on Ubuntu 24.04, both with LANG unset
# and LANG=C.UTF-8 (nightly 36309067888, linux-asan). An entry that stops matching is reported by
# print_suppressions; delete it then.

# 1-2. libX11's process-lifetime caches. SDL_Quit() unloads libX11 (SDL_X11_UnloadSymbols), and libX11
#      still references these blocks from its globals. Once libX11 is unmapped, LSan sees them as
#      unreachable and cannot symbolise libX11's frames ("<unknown module>"), so the nearest frame it can
#      match is SDL's caller. With dlclose() made a no-op these reports disappear: they are not leaks.
#   - The Xlib locale database and input method, from XSetLocaleModifiers() and XOpenIM()
#     (third_party/sdl3/src/video/x11/SDL_x11keyboard.c, X11_InitKeyboard).
leak:X11_InitKeyboard
#   - Xlib's resource-manager quark tables, from XrmInitialize()
#     (third_party/sdl3/src/video/x11/SDL_x11modes.c, X11_GetGlobalContentScale).
leak:X11_GetGlobalContentScale

# 3. libdbus: a read buffer libdbus itself loses when dbus_bus_get_private(DBUS_BUS_SESSION) fails
#    in SDL_DBus_Init() (xvfb-run provides no session bus). Its frames are symbolised in the still-loaded
#    libdbus-1.so.3. SDL_SHUTDOWN_DBUS_ON_QUIT=1 (dbus_shutdown()) does not free it.
leak:_dbus_read
